# CVE-2026-0861 - glibc integer overflow in memalign (REVIEW BY: 2027-03-16)
# CRITICAL per Trivy, but Debian marks as "Minor issue" with <no-dsa>
# Affects libc-bin and libc6; fix shipped in bookworm 2.36-9+deb12u14 per
# tracker (verified 2026-09-16) — keep until image rebuild proves the version.
# Exploitation requires attacker control of BOTH size (near PTRDIFF_MAX) and
# alignment (range [1<<62+1, 1<<63]) arguments to memalign/posix_memalign/aligned_alloc
# Our application doesn't expose memory allocation controls to untrusted input
# Reference: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-0861
CVE-2026-0861

# CVE-2023-2953 - OpenLDAP null pointer dereference in ber_memalloc_x (REVIEW BY: 2027-04-21)
# HIGH severity, no DSA for bookworm (tracker <no-dsa>, verified 2026-09-16)
# Affects libldap-2.5-0 package, a transitive dependency of curl (via libcurl4)
# Not exploitable in our context:
#   1. Our application does not use LDAP functionality
#   2. libldap is only included as a dependency of curl, used for health checks
#   3. The vulnerability requires LDAP operations to trigger
# Reference: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-2953
CVE-2023-2953

# CVE-2026-22695 - libpng denial of service and information disclosure (REVIEW BY: 2027-04-23)
# HIGH severity; fix shipped in bookworm 1.6.39-2+deb12u2 per tracker
# (verified 2026-09-16) — remove once the image rebuild proves the patch.
# Affects libpng16-16 package used by image processing libraries (PIL/Pillow)
# Mitigated by:
#   1. Application validates image input sizes before processing
#   2. Image processing happens in controlled pipeline with trusted FTP sources
#   3. Memory limits enforced at container level
CVE-2026-22695

# CVE-2026-22801 - libpng information disclosure and denial of service (REVIEW BY: 2027-04-23)
# HIGH severity; fix shipped in bookworm 1.6.39-2+deb12u2 per tracker.
# Same package and mitigation as CVE-2026-22695
CVE-2026-22801

# =============================================================================
# Python Package Vulnerabilities - No Fix Available
# =============================================================================

# CVE-2024-23342 - python-ecdsa Minerva timing attack (REVIEW BY: 2027-05-03)
# HIGH severity, no fix planned by upstream maintainer (OSV: unfixed at the
# locked ecdsa 0.19.2, re-verified 2026-09-16)
# python-ecdsa project considers side-channel attacks out of scope
# ecdsa is a transitive dependency via python-jose (JWT library)
# Not exploitable in our context:
#   1. JWT signing uses HMAC (HS256), not ECDSA in our implementation
#   2. Timing attack requires local timing measurement capability
#   3. No ECDH operations or ECDSA signing in production code paths
CVE-2024-23342

# =============================================================================
# Python Package Vulnerabilities - Accepted Risk (fix exists but is
# unreachable through the dependency graph)
# =============================================================================

# CVE-2026-69247 - cryptography PKCS#7 EnvelopedData Bleichenbacher oracle (REVIEW BY: 2027-03-16)
# HIGH, fixed in cryptography 50.0.0 — but the fix is UNREACHABLE: the nemo
# dependency group (project.optional-dependencies + dependency-groups, both
# "data-designer>=0.9.2") pulls data-designer-engine 0.9.2 which pins
# cryptography>=48.0.1,<=49, and 0.9.2 is the engine's latest release
# (registry-checked 2026-09-16). uv resolves one cross-extra environment, so
# the runtime stays on 49.0.0 while the nemo group exists in the lock.
# Not exploitable in our context:
#   1. The oracle requires decrypting attacker-supplied PKCS#7 EnvelopedData;
#      grep over backend/ finds zero uses of PKCS7/EnvelopedData APIs
#   2. cryptography enters only via python-jose (HMAC paths) and pyjwt
#   3. OSV: 50.0.0 clean, 49.0.0 flagged ONLY by this CVE (no other advisories)
# Revisit trigger: data-designer-engine releasing a build that allows
# cryptography>=50; then upgrade and DELETE this entry.
# Reference: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-69247
CVE-2026-69247

